_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nrepro in 4.8 dev 4\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.8.dev4 - Arch Linux #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Fri, 22 May 2026 19:25:09 +0000 on Wayland - Wayland display driver, Single-window, 1 monitor (1920x1080 @ 60.00 Hz) - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - AMD Radeon 780M Graphics (radeonsi, phoenix, ACO, DRM 3.64, 7.0.9-arch2-1) - AMD Ryzen 7 8745HS w/ Radeon 780M Graphics (16 threads) - 28.18 GiB memory - PulseAudio (44100 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\nLikely caused by the \"main screen plugins to docks\" change https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113051\n\nUsing the shortcut `editor/editor_script` does not focus the script editor text area. This really breaks workflows that would switch between the 2D view and the script editor using hotkeys. Both clicking the Script dock and using the keyboard shortcut require clicking in the script text area to actually start typing.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3c92b232-68ba-40ba-98e2-b94fab73ad6a\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Click the script dock at the top of Godot\n2. Notice the caret does not appear in the script area\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/sub